  <h2>Where to shop local in Jackson</h2>
  <p>
    Jackson’s independent commerce is concentrated in a handful of walkable districts. Starting there is the
    simplest way to keep more of your spending in the city:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Fondren</strong> — the arts-and-dining core, with independent cafes, boutiques, and a beloved bookstore.</li>
    <li><strong>Belhaven</strong> — a historic neighborhood with locally owned eateries and specialty shops.</li>
    <li><strong>Midtown</strong> — a maker district of studios, galleries, and small-batch producers.</li>
    <li><strong>Downtown</strong> — locally owned restaurants and services alongside the city’s civic core.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These are <em>districts</em> to explore, not a list of endorsers — where you spend is your call. For a
    verified, source-cited starting point, see our
    <a href="/learn/best-local-businesses-jackson-ms/">guide to Jackson’s best local businesses</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Why local spending gives back more</h2>
  <p>
    “Giving back” isn’t only about donations — it’s about where your dollar goes next. Research popularized by
    Civic Economics and the Institute for Local Self-Reliance finds that roughly
    <strong>${PER_100.localRecirculation} of every $100</strong> spent at an independent local business
    recirculates in the community — local payroll, local suppliers, local giving — versus about
    <strong>${PER_100.chainRecirculation} of every $100</strong> at a national chain. That’s a swing of about
    <strong>${PER_100.localSwing} per $100</strong>, so every dollar you redirect to a local business does
    close to <strong>four times</strong> as much work at home. See the full local picture in our
    <a href="/research/local-giving-index/jackson/">Jackson Local Giving Index</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How Good Circles adds a Jackson nonprofit to every purchase</h2>
  <p>
    When Good Circles opens the Jackson metro in <strong>September 2026</strong>, it makes the “give back” part
    automatic. On every <strong>$100</strong> you spend locally, about
    <strong>{dollars(PER_100.shopperSaves)} comes back to you</strong>, about
    <strong>{dollars(PER_100.nonprofit)} funds a Jackson nonprofit you choose</strong> — paid from the
    merchant’s profit, at no extra cost to you — and the local business keeps 89% of its profit. The
    nonprofits that benefit are elected by neighbors, not picked by the platform.
  </p>
  <p>
